  "releaseNotes": "- Prevent thread-pool starvation during binary checks and codec, format, and pixel-format discovery.\n      - Report progress at low log levels and avoid retaining per-run log-level settings.\n      - Support disabling subtitle and data streams.\n      - Fix relative demux-concat paths, tee output escaping and overwrite handling, and codec names in file-extension mappings.\n      - Propagate failures and cancellation from asynchronous frame and packet probing.\n      - Update Instances to 3.1.0 and expand regression coverage while preserving fork APIs and executable-path overrides.",
